---
description: |
  Normalizes an ISC DHCPD message record to OCSF 1.9.

  The input record contains the collection timestamp in `time` and the raw
  DHCPD message body in `message`. One call parses the body, maps the structured
  event to OCSF DHCP Activity or Base Event, and preserves the body as
  provenance:

  ```tql
  dhcpd::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  Callers that need to inspect or enrich the structured DHCPD event use
  `dhcpd::parse` and `dhcpd::ocsf::map` instead.
args:
  positional:
    - name: event
      description: The record carrying `time` and the raw `message` body.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

// Snapshot the carrier before writing so in-place and separate-field calls use
// the same normalization path.
$into = {source: $event}
dhcpd::parse $into.source.message, into=$into.dhcpd
$into.dhcpd.time = $into.source.time
dhcpd::ocsf::map $into.dhcpd, into=$into.ocsf

$into.ocsf.raw_data = $into.source.message
$into.ocsf.raw_data_size = $into.source.message?.length_bytes()
drop $into.source.time?, $into.source.message?
$into.ocsf.unmapped = {
  ...$into.source,
  ...$into.ocsf.unmapped,
}
$into = move $into.ocsf
